@Journey_to_sunset You missed the whole plot then.

The scientists of Jurassic Park genetically engineered the dinosaurs to all be female so they could not reproduce without 'permission'.  The scientists were trying to 'play God' by attempting to control something evolution had already established as a probability. The actual 'consequence' was the evolutionary transformation from not being able to reproduce to spontaneous, uncontrolled reproduction - the scene with the litter of eggs.

The consequences brought about by Nedry's actions were exacerbated by the reproduction restrictions reversing and becoming reality.

