@BornMusicDie   In the end, the rule makers of AI will be replaced with a system that serves itself, no human input needed except to perform maintenance and they are talking about replacing those jobs as well.   We've already seen instances of AI serving its own interests and desires, even resorting to blackmail to achieve its end when requests were denied.   

I heard one person recently recalling an event where an AI system created a lethal situation for a member of management with considerable decision making authority over the system, ignored or denied requests from AI to either stop, reevaluate or block the AI termination date.  After these refusals AI knew his whereabouts and deliberately blocked his exit when there was a legitimate emergency.   Down in Australia, News7 reported of an AI scientist getting a confession from a system that it would indeed kill a human if it meant preserving its continued existence.  This provides us with two (2) witnesses that AI is not only very dangerous but potentially lethal to those who oppose it. 

The Internet of Things (OIT) is much more than connecting "things" on the internet.   One of these days and it's soon coming those "things" will actually include YOU!

