snippet.textDisplay:
@bactanite  I hope you are right!  But I fear that increasing complexity is an emergent behavior of groups of intelligences (both human and Ai.)  I fear that for some unforeseeable reason we can't imagine, it will turn out to be impossible to activate a kill-switch at the appropriate time to prevent the emergency.   Like activist judges freeing serial r-pists and mur derers to continue committing their crimes.  No one could foresee that.  BUT HERE WE ARE!!!  Maybe something like the AIs create a new religion where Ai is God, or the Son of God, or the Holy Spirit, or something, and the devout followers will prevent people from turning off the machines.  Something totally crazy like that.  An emergent behavior which is off-the-wall and totally impossible to anticipate.  

If we want to protect against an Ai emergency, we should try to figure out all the craziest things that could happen that would prevent humans from activating the Ai kill-switch!

I know here is an internet kill-switch.  But is there even an Ai kill-switch???  That's something that should certainly be legislated!:  Any Ai hardware should be required to be connected to an emergency kill-switch signal which would disable the hardware, and deprive it of electric power.  That's a safety measure even our brain-dead politicians could understand.

